## Data-Driven Styling & Expressions

### Expressions Overview
Expressions define formulas for computing property values using operators. Full reference: https://docs.mapbox.com/style-spec/reference/expressions/

**Expression Categories:**
- **Lookup:** `get`, `has`, `in`, `at`, `length`
- **Decision:** `match`, `case`, `coalesce`
- **Math:** `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `%`, `^`, `sqrt`, `log10`, `abs`, `round`, `ceil`, `floor`, `min`, `max`
- **String:** `concat`, `downcase`, `upcase`, `slice`
- **Type:** `to-string`, `to-number`, `to-boolean`, `to-color`, `typeof`
- **Interpolation:** `interpolate`, `step`
- **Zoom:** `zoom`
- **Feature:** `feature-state`, `geometry-type`, `id`, `properties`

### Style Across Zoom Range
Linear, exponential, cubic-bezier, or step interpolation.

```json
{
  "circle-radius": [
    "interpolate",
    ["linear"],
    ["zoom"],
    10, 2,
    15, 5,
    20, 10
  ]
}
```

**Legacy syntax (still supported):**
```json
{
  "circle-radius": {
    "stops": [[10, 2], [15, 5], [20, 10]]
  }
}
```

### Style Across Data Range
Interpolate based on numeric property values.

```json
{
  "fill-color": [
    "interpolate",
    ["linear"],
    ["get", "population"],
    0, "#fff",
    100000, "#ff0",
    1000000, "#f00"
  ]
}
```

### Style With Data Conditions
Conditional logic based on property values.

```json
{
  "fill-color": [
    "match",
    ["get", "class"],
    "park", "#0f0",
    "hospital", "#f0f",
    "school", "#ff0",
    "#ccc"
  ]
}
```

### Complex Expression Patterns

**Combine zoom and data:**
```json
{
  "circle-radius": [
    "interpolate",
    ["exponential", 1.5],
    ["zoom"],
    10, ["*", ["get", "value"], 0.1],
    15, ["*", ["get", "value"], 0.5],
    20, ["*", ["get", "value"], 1.0]
  ]
}
```

**Conditional with fallback:**
```json
{
  "text-field": [
    "coalesce",
    ["get", "name_en"],
    ["get", "name"],
    "Unknown"
  ]
}
```

**Case-based logic:**
```json
{
  "circle-color": [
    "case",
    [">", ["get", "temperature"], 30], "#f00",
    [">", ["get", "temperature"], 20], "#ff0",
    [">", ["get", "temperature"], 10], "#0f0",
    "#00f"
  ]
}
```

